1. FEM.py :: beta_range()
-------------------------

Derived from dwave-neal (now dwave-samplers), neal/sampler.py ::
_default_ising_beta_range, as of version 0.5.x.

    Copyright 2018 D-Wave Systems Inc.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
    Source: https://github.com/dwavesystems/dwave-neal

Modifications made:
  - renamed from _default_ising_beta_range to beta_range;
  - the cold-temperature target excitation rate was changed from 1% to 0.01%,
    i.e. cold_beta = log(100)/min_delta_energy became
    cold_beta = log(10000)/min_delta_energy.
Otherwise the function is unchanged, including its docstring and comments.

Note that upstream has since rewritten this function substantially; the version
here descends from the older one.


2. bnn_as_qubo.py :: le_zero_constraint_to_eq_zero_constraint()
---------------------------------------------------------------

Adapted from qubovert, qubovert/_pcbo.py :: PCBO.add_constraint_le_zero.

    Copyright 2020 Joseph T. Iosue
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
    Source: https://github.com/jtiosue/qubovert

Modifications made:
  - rewritten as a free function that builds and returns a fresh qv.PCBO,
    rather than a method mutating self;
  - the upstream _append_constraint("le", P) bookkeeping and the "if not lam"
    early return are dropped, and the Lagrange multiplier is fixed at 1 rather
    than taken as an argument;
  - in the general branch, the slack-padded polynomial is added to the model
    directly (model += P) instead of being routed through
    add_constraint_eq_zero(...) followed by _pop_constraint("eq"). Upstream
    squares the polynomial into a penalty term; this version does not, which is
    the point of the function -- it hands back an equality-form constraint for
    the caller to penalise.

The ancilla loop, the min_val / max_val branch structure, the two
QUBOVertWarning messages and the "don't mutate the P" comment are carried over
essentially verbatim.


